 while issa rae is known for her  role in the hbo series insecure while  most of the film's plot details have yet  to be confirmed we do have an official  synopsis miles morales returns for the  next chapter of the oscar-winning  spider-verse saga an epic adventure that  will transport brooklyn's full-time  friendly neighborhood spider-man across  the multiverse to join forces with gwen  stacy and a new team of spider people to  face off with a villain more powerful  than anything they've ever encountered  the two co-writers for the film  christopher miller and phil lord noted  that every dimension looks and feels  radically different from all the others  they all look like they were drawn by a  different artist so we can expect to see  many different art styles used  throughout the movie as well as spider  people that we have yet to see before  the two also teased that the events of  spider-man no way home could have  implications for miles and gwen in the  upcoming sony picture in the recently  released teaser trailer miles and gwen  look older than they did in the first  film so it's likely been a year or two  since they said their goodbyes and into  the spiderverse we also know that miles  will be jumping across universes the  opposite of what happened in the first  film when all the other spider people  came to his universe as for the movie's  main villain i don't think it's likely  to be spider-man 2099 even though he's  seen wrestling with miles in the teaser  trailer it's likely that he's simply  confused about who miles is or that he's  trying to recruit him to fight against  the film's main villain the movie's  villain could be one of many including  the spot green goblin doctor octopus  venom tyler stone craven the hunter or  even another spider-man variant such as  the superior spider-man which i actually  made a video on that'll be linked at the  end of this video part 2 of across the  spider-verse is expected to release  sometime during 2023 and we can